   "title": "USB wall charger",
   "subtitle": "PS1 \u2014 UL-listed 5 V phone charger",
   "w": 146,
   "h": 88,
   "notes": "Mains prongs are drawn in mains red because the AC side sits at line potential; the USB output is drawn in low-volt blue. The white cube between them IS the isolation argument (a listed charger is a certified reinforced-isolation AC-DC supply), so keep the two colours visibly separated on any sheet that places this part. No current rating is printed: the BOM specifies only >=500 mA, 5 V. Which outlet feeds it is an open decision in the BOM, so no plug type or mains voltage is marked either.",
