  {
   "id": "key-fob",
   "title": "433 MHz key fob (opened)",
   "subtitle": "KA1 fob half \u2014 board silkscreened CYS02-E2",
   "w": 170,
   "h": 100,
   "notes": "The fob out of its case, as it is on the bench: opened and pigtailed to a six-way connector. Cell holder and buttons are drawn on one face for legibility \u2014 on the real board the coin-cell holder and the encoder are on opposite faces (see hardware/photos/). Conductor colours follow the pigtail table in hardware/schematic/WIRING.md, which is read off photographs and NOT METERED: which pair is the ON button, which conductor the encoder sees, and the cell voltage are all unrecorded. For that reason no pin carries a power or GND signal \u2014 the fob rail must not be auto-netted to the ESP32's, and the optocoupler exists precisely so the two grounds are never tied. Earlier revisions asserted a 12 V A23 cell; the board carries a coin-cell holder, so no voltage is drawn or printed.",
