  {
   "id": "pushbutton-panel",
   "title": "Panel-mount pushbutton",
   "subtitle": "Momentary, normally open \u2014 acknowledge button on GPIO27",
   "w": 150,
   "h": 96,
   "notes": "Drawn as a real panel button: bezel and cap in front of the enclosure wall (the light slab), threaded barrel through the hole, panel nut and two solder tags behind. SELV throughout \u2014 nothing here is at mains potential, so no red appears. Both tags are drawn identical and the pins are unpolarised: the firmware idles GPIO27 high on its internal pullup and a press pulls it low, so either tag can take GPIO27 and the other GND. No cap legend is engraved because the switch is a scrounged part and no marking is established.",
